      "kind": "BODY",
      "characters": 1430,
      "text": "Representative Import Fixture for Apple Pages\nThis document is intentionally ordinary: it is meant to be opened in Apple Pages and saved as a native .pages file for importer tests.\n1. Body text and inline formatting\nPurpose. Use this fixture to validate basic text extraction, paragraph ordering, character runs, and style preservation. It includes bold, italic, underlined, and code-like text: let importer = PagesImporter().\nUnicode coverage: café, naïve, coöperate, emojis 🚀 ✅, smart quotes “like this”, em dash —, non-breaking spaces, and CJK text: 日本語・中文・한국어.\n2. Lists\nPlain paragraph before list should remain separate.\nFirst unordered item with a longer line that wraps naturally.\nSecond unordered item with punctuation: a/b, 10–20%, $1,234.56.\nFirst ordered item\nSecond ordered item\nThird ordered item with nested-looking text: 1.1 not actually nested\n3. Table\nThe table has a header row, mixed alignment, empty cells, currency-like text, and multiline text.\n￼\n4. Link and image\nExternal link: Apple Developer Documentation — useful for checking URL extraction.\n￼\nFigure 1. Embedded chart image generated for this fixture.\n\u00045. Landscape section and wider table\nThis page checks section handling, orientation, headers/footers, and wide tables after Pages conversion.\n￼\n6. Dates and formula\nThis page checks dates and formula\n￼\n7. End marker\nEND_OF_PAGES_IMPORT_FIXTURE — use this marker to verify full-document extraction."
    },
